If you're using VS Code

Your current folder is:

C:\Users\pande\Dropbox\Yuvaintern_week2\week3

Open that folder in VS Code and use the terminal.

First run:

git init

Then:

git add .

Then:

git commit -m "Complete Week 3 Logistics EDA"

Then create a new empty repository on GitHub named:

week3-logistics-eda

After creating it, GitHub will give you commands similar to:

git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/week3-logistics-eda.git
git push -u origin main

Don't copy my URL literally—use the repository URL GitHub gives you.

If you want, send me a screenshot of your GitHub new repository page, and I'll tell you exactly what to click/type next, one step at a time.

