README.md
Logistics Performance — Exploratory Data Analysis
📌 Project Overview

This project presents an Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) of logistics delivery performance data.

The analysis focuses on understanding delivery time, delivery cost, distance, package weight, delivery ratings, delivery status, delays, and operational segments such as regions, delivery modes, delivery partners, and vehicle types.

The objective is to convert raw logistics records into clear statistical insights that can support operational monitoring and further analysis.

📊 Dataset
Records: 25,000
Columns: 16
Missing values: 0
Duplicate rows: 0
Main Variables
delivery_id
delivery_partner
package_type
vehicle_type
delivery_mode
region
weather_condition
distance_km
package_weight_kg
delivery_time_hours
expected_time_hours
delayed
delivery_status
delivery_rating
delivery_cost
distance_category
📈 Key Performance Metrics
Metric	Result
Average Delivery Time	6.25 hours
Average Delivery Cost	864.94
Average Delivery Rating	3.67
Delivered	73.32%
Delayed	21.36%
Failed	5.31%
🔎 EDA Performed
1. Data Quality Analysis
Dataset structure and dimensions
Missing-value analysis
Duplicate-row analysis
Data-type and numerical-field checks
2. Descriptive Statistics

Calculated:

Mean
Median
Standard deviation
Minimum and maximum
Quartiles
Interquartile Range (IQR)
3. Distribution Analysis

Created distributions for:

Delivery time
Delivery cost
Delivery distance
4. Outlier Analysis

Used the 1.5 × IQR rule to identify potential outliers in:

Distance
Package weight
Delivery time
Delivery cost

Potential outliers were treated as observations requiring investigation rather than automatically being considered errors.

5. Relationship Analysis

Analyzed:

Distance vs delivery time
Distance vs delivery cost
Actual vs expected delivery time
Correlations among numerical logistics variables
6. Operational Segmentation

Compared:

Average delivery time by region
Average delivery cost by delivery mode
Average delivery rating by delivery partner
Delivery records by vehicle type
Delay rate by region
