💡 Operational Insights

The EDA provides a baseline for monitoring logistics performance across time, cost, quality, and delays.

The analysis can help logistics teams:

Identify unusually long deliveries for further investigation.
Monitor delivery cost patterns across operating modes.
Compare regional delivery performance.
Track service quality through delivery ratings.
Monitor delay rates using normalized percentages.
Identify relationships between distance and operational performance.
Use outlier analysis to investigate exceptional deliveries.
🚀 Possible Future Improvements

Future analysis could include:

Time-series analysis of delivery performance.
Predictive modeling for late-delivery risk.
Route-level performance analysis.
Cost-per-kilometre analysis.
Weather impact analysis.
Delivery-partner benchmarking.
Interactive Power BI dashboard integration.
📄 Report

A detailed DOC report containing the methodology, statistical analysis, visualizations, findings, and recommendations is included in the project.

Project: Week 3 — Exploratory Data Analysis on Logistics Performance